# =============================================================================
# .NET Study Case — Cenários de desenvolvimento para Ajuste 2 (RBAC)
# PRÉ-REQUISITO: Direct access grants habilitado no gateway-client (só dev).
# Selecionar environment "dev" no Run with antes de executar.
# Ordem obrigatória: rodar os 3 requests do Bloco 1 primeiro, um por um.
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# BLOCO 1 — Obtenção de tokens (rodar primeiro, um por um)
# =============================================================================

### [TOKEN] Service account (gateway-client — sem role user/admin)
POST {{realm}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}

> {%
    client.global.set("saToken", response.body.access_token);
%}

### [TOKEN] testuser (role: user)
POST {{realm}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}&username=testuser&password={{testUserPassword}}

> {%
    client.global.set("testuserToken", response.body.access_token);
%}

### [TOKEN] adminuser (role: admin)
POST {{realm}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}&username=adminuser&password={{adminUserPassword}}

> {%
    client.global.set("adminuserToken", response.body.access_token);
%}

# =============================================================================
# BLOCO 2 — Autenticação básica (regressão)
# =============================================================================

### [1] Sem token → 401
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies

### [2] Token inválido (assinatura corrompida) → 401
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJmYWtlIn0.assinatura_invalida

# =============================================================================
# BLOCO 3 — RBAC: role USER (testuser)
# =============================================================================

### [3] testuser → GET /anomalies → 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies
Authorization: Bearer {{testuserToken}}

### [4] testuser → GET /anomalies/1 → 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies/1
Authorization: Bearer {{testuserToken}}

### [5] testuser → GET /anomalies/99 → 404 (passou RBAC, recurso não existe)
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies/99
Authorization: Bearer {{testuserToken}}

### [6] testuser → GET /anomalies/report → 403 (role user, BLOQUEADO)
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies/report
Authorization: Bearer {{testuserToken}}

# =============================================================================
# BLOCO 4 — RBAC: role ADMIN (adminuser)
# =============================================================================

### [7] adminuser → GET /anomalies → 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies
Authorization: Bearer {{adminuserToken}}

### [8] adminuser → GET /anomalies/2 → 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies/2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminuserToken}}

### [9] adminuser → GET /anomalies/report → 200 (M2M completo)
# gateway → sentinel (valida JWT admin) →
#   KeycloakTokenService obtém token via client_credentials →
#   descobre audit-service via Consul →
#   chama audit-service via mTLS com token service →
#   audit valida policy ServiceOnly → retorna logs →
#   sentinel compõe anomalias + audit logs
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies/report
Authorization: Bearer {{adminuserToken}}

# =============================================================================
# BLOCO 5 — Service account sem role de usuário
# =============================================================================

### [10] service account → GET /anomalies → 403 (sem role user/admin)
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies
Authorization: Bearer {{saToken}}

### [11] service account → GET /anomalies/report → 403 (sem role admin)
GET {{gateway}}/api/sentinel-service/anomalies/report
Authorization: Bearer {{saToken}}